---
// src/components/ui/DashboardPreview.astro
// Bento-grid "product dashboard" visual for the homepage hero — converted
// from the approved hero-dashboard-preview.html mockup. This is a fixed,
// content-complete, single-purpose component built only for Hero.astro's
// hero section; it is NOT a general-purpose primitive and isn't meant to
// be reused elsewhere or extended with props for other content. Renders
// only the bento grid itself — the "Monopol" eyebrow and headline in the
// source preview were placeholder text for the standalone mockup and are
// intentionally dropped here; the real eyebrow/H1 belong to Hero.astro
// per this task's brief. Not yet wired into Hero.astro — that's a
// separate stage.
//
// AutomationNotificationCard.astro is untouched by this file and is not
// used here — this component owns its own card markup directly since the
// preview's cards (fixed layout, no expand/collapse, no icon slot) don't
// match that component's collapsible-notification contract.
//
// GRID RESTRUCTURE (per brief item 1): the preview's 6th filler cell
// ("20,000+ users already joined" in the bottom-right grid slot) is
// dropped — that figure doesn't exist anywhere in SITE_IDENTITY_AND_AEO.md
// (Section 3 gives a 50-person beta cohort, pre-launch) and would ship a
// fabricated stat. Rather than leave the bottom-right cell empty, the grid
// is restructured to 5 cells: the Client Portal card (originally 2/3-width
// in the bottom row) now spans the full width of row 3 (`lg:col-span-3`),
// so the 3x3 grid is fully and intentionally occupied with no dead cell
// and no invented replacement content.
//
// GRID GEOMETRY FIX (bento rebalance — "Lower cost" card): the original
// `lg:row-span-2` on card 4 relied on the browser's sparse auto-placement
// dropping it into the middle column at row 2 (col 1 was pinned by card 1's
// own row-span-2), which left column 3 empty for two full rows — a tall,
// narrow numeral card floating next to dead space. Fix: card 4 drops
// `lg:row-span-2` and takes `lg:col-span-2` instead (still a plain
// standard-scale utility, no arbitrary value). With card 1 occupying
// column 1 across rows 1–2, sparse auto-placement now naturally slots
// cards 2 and 3 into columns 2–3 of row 1, and card 4's 2-column span is
// the *only* opening left in row 2 (columns 2–3) — so it lands there
// automatically with zero explicit `grid-column`/`grid-row` coordinates
// needed. Net result: card 4 is now short and wide instead of tall and
// narrow, every cell in the 3x3 area is filled, and no other card's span
// had to change — cards 1, 2, 3, and 5 keep their original classes
// untouched; only card 4's span utilities changed. Confirmed this still
// degrades cleanly below `lg`: `lg:row-span-2` and `lg:col-span-2` are both
// breakpoint-gated, so below `lg` every card reverts to the implicit
// `col-span-1 row-span-1` on the single-column grid and stacks in DOM
// order (1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5) exactly as before.
//
// ⚠️ Flag — gradient icon badges: the preview's pipeline/portal icon
// badges use CSS gradients (`linear-gradient(135deg,#2f6bff,#5a8bff)` and
// an ink gradient). DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Section 1 reserves gradients for the
// flow-rail signature element only ("Reserved — not for general use.").
// Mapped both badges to solid fills instead: pipeline → `bg-blue-600`
// (fixed accent), portal → `bg-ink` (matches the Elevated/filled-dark
// convention already used elsewhere, e.g. AutomationNotificationCard's
// icon chips). No gradient anywhere in this file outside that convention.
//
// ⚠️ Flag — card 4's background wash: the preview gives the pricing card
// a subtle `linear-gradient(165deg,#ffffff,#f6f8ff)` panel background.
// DESIGN_SYSTEM.md doesn't approve a general card-background gradient
// (again, gradients are reserved for the flow-rail only), so this was
// dropped in favor of flat `bg-white`, matching every other card. Purely
// a richness/polish loss, not a structural change.
//
// ⚠️ Flag — dot-grid placement (card 4 corner texture): the preview's
// `.price-dots` corner texture is visually identical to DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
// Section 4's approved Dot-Grid Texture technique (same radial-gradient
// `rail`-color pattern), so it's implemented here using that same
// approved bracket-notation pattern with a corner mask rather than an
// invented texture. BUT Section 4 scopes dot-grid to "hero only, one per
// page" and Section 7.5 says never stack two decorative patterns in the
// same area. Since this component is destined for Hero.astro, and I
// haven't been asked to inspect what background texture Hero.astro
// itself already uses, this card's corner dot-grid may end up being a
// second dot-grid instance on the same page/section once wired in —
// confirm at integration time whether Hero.astro already has one, and
// drop this card's instance if so.
//
// ⚠️ Flag — sub-heading size unification: the preview uses three
// different ad-hoc h4 sizes (17px / 15px / 17px) for the "Replaces 5+
// apps," "Project Timesheet," and "Client Portal" card headers. None of
// these map to a named DESIGN_SYSTEM.md type-scale entry (only Feature H3
// at text-xl is named for card headings). Unified all three to `text-lg
// font-semibold text-ink` — the nearest standard Tailwind step below
// Feature H3 — rather than approximating three separate arbitrary pixel
// values.
//
// ⚠️ Flag — card 3's stat number: "5–8 hrs/week" is a secondary stat, not
// the page's one allowed oversized Display Numeral (that treatment —
// `font-display font-semibold text-amber-500` at `text-6xl`–`text-8xl`,
// one per page max — is spent on card 4's "50–70%" instead, since that's
// the closer match to the preview's largest/boldest number and to keep
// only one amber numeral on the page). Card 3's number instead uses
// `font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink` — display font for
// numeral confidence, but sized and colored down since it isn't the
// page's one big-numeral moment.
//
// ⚠️ Flag — qualifier pill colors (brief item 6): "(beta target)" and
// "(target)" must stay visible, non-removable text per the brief. Rather
// than inventing new pill styling, each was mapped to the closest already
// -approved badge token based on the preview's own color choice: card 3's
// amber/gold pill → the existing Warning badge
// (`bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 ring-amber-600/20`, Section 1 functional
// colors) — read here as "unverified projection, treat with caution."
// Card 4's neutral grey pill → the Neutral/Category Pill (Section 3)
// — read as a plain caveat label rather than a warning. Both are literal,
// non-hidden text content, never a tooltip or title attribute.
//
// Body copy sizes: mapped to DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's *named* type-scale roles
// (Body Paragraph `text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed`, Small/Caption
// `text-sm text-ink/50`) exactly as specified, rather than hand-picking a
// closer pixel match to the preview's 12.5–15px custom sizes — this
// keeps every text style traceable to a named token instead of an
// eyeballed approximation.
//
// bg-white vs bg-paper: DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's card specs (Standard Feature
// Card, Elevated Card) both default to `bg-paper`, but this component
// uses `bg-white` for every card surface instead. Reasoning: this bento
// grid is meant to read as a crisp, self-contained "product dashboard"
// floating over whatever background Hero.astro paints behind it (gradient
// wash / dot-grid / paper — all warm-toned), the same way Section 4's
// "Section Background Rhythm" describes `bg-white` as "the occasional
// crisp break" against the paper baseline. It also matches the preview's
// own `--card: #ffffff` more precisely than paper's warm off-white would.
// Confirm this reads correctly once actually placed against Hero.astro's
// specific background at integration time.
//
// The preview's custom toggle-switch (built via a `::after` pseudo-
// element in the source HTML) is rebuilt here as two plain nested spans
// using only standard-scale Tailwind position/size utilities
// (`h-6 w-11`, `right-0.5`, `top-0.5`, `h-5 w-5`) — no pseudo-elements, no
// inline style. It's decorative only (no real on/off state to convey
// beyond the "Manual overhead" pill's own text), so it's `aria-hidden`.
//
// No required props — this is a fixed, content-complete block. `class`
// is accepted for outer placement/spacing only, matching the passthrough
// pattern already used on AutomationNotificationCard.

import { ClipboardList, MessageSquareWarning } from 'lucide-astro';

export interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<div class:list={['grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-3', className]} data-dashboard-preview>

  <!-- Card 1: Endless Admin Chores (tall, left column, spans both top rows) -->
  <div class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm lg:row-span-2">
    <div class="mb-5 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-600 shadow-sm">
      <ClipboardList class="w-6 h-6 text-white" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true" />
    </div>
    <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">Trapped in Admin Work</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink/50">0 billable hours</p>
    <p class="mt-3 flex-grow text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Every accepted proposal triggers a mountain of unpaid prep: custom agreements, invoice reminders, and shared drives. It feels like a full-time job before work even starts.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-rail pt-5">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-red-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-red-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-red-600/20">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-red-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Manual overhead
      </span>
      <span class="relative inline-block h-6 w-11 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-red-600" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="absolute right-0.5 top-0.5 h-5 w-5 rounded-full bg-white shadow"></span>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Card 2: Too Many Disconnected Apps (middle column, top row) -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
    <h4 class="mb-4 text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Too Many Disconnected Apps</h4>
    <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-rail/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/70 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-sm bg-blue-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Agreements
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-rail/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/70 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-sm bg-blue-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Billing
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-rail/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/70 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-sm bg-blue-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Task Boards
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-rail/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/70 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-sm bg-blue-600" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Client DMs
      </span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-transparent px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/50 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">
        + 4 more
      </span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink/50">A different app for every little task. You end up wasting half your time switching between tabs and copying the same info everywhere.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Card 3: Wasted on Payment Chasing (middle column, bottom row) -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
    <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Wasted on Payment Chasing</h4>
    <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-ink/50">Non-billable hours</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <span class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">5–8 hrs/week</span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-red-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-red-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-red-600/20">Unpaid Time</span>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/50">Following up on unpaid invoices, hearing "it's in process," and losing days waiting for payouts.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Card 4: Lower cost / pricing (short, wide — spans both middle/right columns, row 2 only) -->
  <div class="relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm lg:col-span-2">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-2 -top-2 h-24 w-24 opacity-40 [background-image:radial-gradient(theme(colors.rail)_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:12px_12px] [mask-image:linear-gradient(225deg,black_10%,transparent_65%)]" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-3">
      <span class="font-display text-6xl font-semibold text-amber-500">30–40%</span>
    </div>
    <span class="mt-2 inline-flex w-fit items-center rounded-full bg-rail/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/70 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">SaaS Bloat</span>
    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">Lost to Hidden Fees & Cuts</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 flex-grow text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Marketplace commissions and heavy per-seat software fees that eat into a big chunk of your actual earnings.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Card 5: Messy Client Communication & Scope Creep (bottom row, full width — absorbs the dropped 6th cell, see file-header note) -->
  <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-4 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:flex-row sm:items-center lg:col-span-3">
    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-ink shadow-sm">
      <MessageSquareWarning class="w-6 h-6 text-paper" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true" />
    </div>
    <div class="flex-grow">
      <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Messy Client Communication & Scope Creep</h4>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/50">Files scattered across WhatsApp, email, and DMs, unpaid extra revisions, and constantly explaining project status to clients.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="inline-flex flex-shrink-0 items-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-full bg-rail/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink/70 ring-1 ring-inset ring-ink/10">Zero Boundaries</span>
  </div>

</div>
